Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/libtests/pngstest.c
Line: 3621
Function: main
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: --tmpfile handling copies the prefix with strncpy(tmpf, argv[c], sizeof(tmpf)-1) after only checking strlen(argv[c]) >= sizeof(tmpf). If the prefix length is exactly sizeof(tmpf)-1, tmpf is not NUL-terminated. Subsequent use of tmpf as a C string can read past the end of the buffer, causing an out-of-bounds read.

